From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: mxs-dma: do not reset the block on resume

The system resume callback ran mxs_dma_init() again, which resets the
whole APBH/APBX block with stmp_reset_block(). Client drivers keep their
channels allocated across suspend (i2c-mxs requests its channel at probe,
the SAIF PCM at registration), so the reset pulls the channel state out
from under them. After resume the first DMA transfer on the I2C0 channel
still finished, and every later one stalled: i2c-mxs timed out with
-ETIMEDOUT after 1 s. Resetting the channel alone did not bring it back.

The block keeps its power and register state in suspend, as the
upstream driver (which has no system sleep callbacks) relies on. Use
pm_runtime_force_suspend()/pm_runtime_force_resume(), which only stop
and restart the clock and keep the runtime PM state balanced.

Seen on Brain PW-A9300 with s2idle: after resume, i2c-mxs PIO transfers
(up to 4 bytes read, 6 bytes write) still worked, so the keyboard and
touch panel on I2C0 were fine, but the YMU818 codec init failed at its
first long write and audio playback failed with -ETIMEDOUT. I2C reads of
8 and 16 bytes (DMA) timed out every time.

Checked on PW-A9300: s2idle, wake by key, then 8- and 16-byte I2C reads
(DMA) worked and the YMU818 init and a 3 s playback succeeded.

diff --git a/drivers/dma/mxs-dma.c b/drivers/dma/mxs-dma.c
index 1b0c3ef5e..a19eaa2a8 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/mxs-dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/mxs-dma.c
@@ -902,29 +902,6 @@ static int mxs_dma_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_PM_SLEEP
-static int mxs_dma_pm_suspend(struct device *dev)
-{
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
-
-	return ret;
-}
-
-static int mxs_dma_pm_resume(struct device *dev)
-{
-	struct mxs_dma_engine *mxs_dma = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-	int ret;
-
-	ret = mxs_dma_init(mxs_dma);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-
-	return 0;
-}
-#endif
-
 int mxs_dma_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct mxs_dma_engine *mxs_dma = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -950,7 +927,12 @@ int mxs_dma_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops mxs_dma_pm_ops = {
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(mxs_dma_runtime_suspend, mxs_dma_runtime_resume, NULL)
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(mxs_dma_pm_suspend, mxs_dma_pm_resume)
+	/*
+	 * The block keeps its power and state in suspend. Do not reset it on
+	 * resume: the I2C and SAIF drivers keep their channels allocated, and
+	 * a block reset under them leaves the channels unusable.
+	 */
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 };
 
 static struct platform_driver mxs_dma_driver = {
